    id:'d-chabahar', slug:'chabahar-port-long-term-contract', attribution:'bjp', government:'NDA III', year:2024, date:'13 May 2024', kind:'Treaty', sector:'Ports, connectivity & sanctions', countries:['India','Iran','Afghanistan'], title:'Chabahar — a ten-year port bet inside a sanctions environment', deck:'The contract gives India a long-term operating role at Shahid Beheshti terminal and a route toward Afghanistan and Central Asia, but finance, rail links and sanctions exposure shape its real utility.', status:'Long-term operating contract signed',
    overview:'India Ports Global Limited and Iran’s Port and Maritime Organization signed the long-term main contract to equip and operate the Shahid Beheshti terminal at Chabahar. The port gives India a route to Afghanistan and Central Asia that bypasses Pakistan and connects conceptually with the International North–South Transport Corridor.',
