    id:'d-climate', slug:'paris-agreement-and-international-solar-alliance', attribution:'bjp', government:'NDA I–II', year:2016, date:'2015–2022', kind:'Treaty', sector:'Climate & energy diplomacy', countries:['Multilateral'], title:'Paris commitments and the Solar Alliance — global ambition with nationally chosen delivery', deck:'India’s climate pledge is internationally recorded but nationally determined; the Solar Alliance is a cooperation institution, not a supranational power regulator.', status:'Paris Agreement ratified; updated NDC active',
    overview:'India ratified the Paris Agreement and submitted nationally determined climate commitments covering emissions intensity, non-fossil electricity capacity and forest carbon sinks. India and France also launched the International Solar Alliance, later opened beyond the tropics, to mobilise cooperation, finance and deployment. Neither instrument directly writes domestic power-sector law; implementation runs through national policy, budgets, regulation and investment.',
    provisions:[{title:'Nationally determined targets',detail:'Paris requires successive national contributions and reporting, but each Party chooses the content and domestic measures of its NDC.'},{title:'Intensity, capacity and sink metrics',detail:'India’s updated NDC uses emissions intensity of GDP, cumulative electric-power installed capacity from non-fossil sources, and an additional forest/tree carbon sink.'},{title:'Equity and development framing',detail:'India’s submissions place climate action in the context of sustainable development, poverty eradication and differentiated responsibility.'},{title:'ISA cooperation',detail:'The Solar Alliance framework creates an intergovernmental platform for programmes, finance mobilisation, capacity and common solar deployment challenges.'}],
    benefits:['Makes domestic energy transition legible internationally while retaining national choice over policy instruments.','ISA gives India agenda-setting influence in solar cooperation among developing and climate-vulnerable countries.'],
    tradeoffs:['An installed-capacity share is not the same as the share of electricity actually generated, which depends on utilisation and grid integration.','Forest-carbon targets can create land and measurement conflicts if plantation quantity substitutes for ecosystem quality or community rights.'],
